  This definition file is used for resolving initial economy prices and popularity.

  initial_price is an optional positive whole-GP starting price, clamped to economy minimums.
  Existing saved prices always win. Omit it to use the item's normal definition value.

  initial_popularity is an optional nonnegative integer in effective-sample units (default 0).
  It affects bot selection only, never price resistance or saved sample counts. Its contribution
  halves after that many real samples and gradually fades thereafter.
*/
